The three reviewers’ comments are largely consistent. They raise concerns regarding:
(1) motivation;
(2) problem formulation;
(3) novelty and positioning of the contributions—particularly the lack of comparison with Hierarchical Federated Learning (HFL) and unclear delineation among contributions related to stochastic proximal point methods, client-sampling strategies, and cohort reuse;
(4) practicality of the proposed setup, including the cohort-reuse assumption and the communication-cost model;
(5) reliance on a strong convexity assumption in the theoretical analysis;
(6) limited experimental scale; and
(7) clarity of presentation.
